## Writing a New Thesis

Create a JSON config in `books/`. Required sections:

```
meta            â€” title, date, claim, budget
nodes           â€” observable states (event, price, indicator, deadline, gate, constraint, conditional, reversal)
edges           â€” causal channels with mechanism, lag, strength (0-1)
instruments     â€” portfolio positions mapped to nodes (monthly alloc, ref, targets, stops)
scenarios       â€” what-if overrides with probability-weighted portfolio impact
cascadePhases   â€” 5-phase tracker (shock â†’ transmission â†’ amplification â†’ policyResponse â†’ resolution)
marketFields    â€” editable market data inputs
fetchSymbols    â€” Yahoo Finance symbols for --fetch
rules           â€” trading discipline
provenance      â€” sources, methodology, limitations
```

Validate with `--dry-run`, generate with `-o`, export state with `--export-state`. See the two existing configs for complete examples.

