      "priceAction": {
        "djiaStart": 294,
        "djiaTrough": 41,
        "tradeCollapse": "-65% (1929-1934)",
        "unemploymentPeak": "25%"
      },
      "lessons": [
        "Retaliation is automatic and escalatory â€” 24 countries responded within 2 years.",
        "Global trade collapsed 65% â€” the tariffs deepened the Depression, they didn't cause it.",
        "Both episodes started during expansion (1929 growth, 2024-25 growth), not recession.",
        "Agricultural exporters were the hardest hit â€” farm income collapsed.",
        "The political feedback loop delayed repeal by 4 years despite obvious damage."
      ],
      "notes": "Structural analog: broad tariff increase during expansion, met with retaliation, deepening existing stress. The 2026 effective tariff rate (13.7%) is the highest since Smoot-Hawley. Key difference: modern economy is services-heavy and supply-chain-integrated."
    },
